# GitNexus walker ignore file (honored by gitnexus' ignore-service in
# addition to .gitignore). Use this to scope GitNexus' index without
# adding paths to .gitignore (which git itself respects).
#
# gui/src-tauri/ is intentionally **out of the cargo workspace** — it's
# a standalone Tauri shell that ships separately and uses different
# build/runtime tooling. Including it in the main GitNexus graph would
# (a) inflate impact-analysis blast radius across an unrelated build
# graph, and (b) confuse symbol resolution when the same crate names
# appear in both trees.
#
# To index the Tauri app on its own (registered as a distinct repo in
# the GitNexus registry), run from the repo root:
#
#   npx -y gitnexus@latest analyze gui/src-tauri/ --skip-agents-md
gui/src-tauri/
